{
    desc => q{:set tabstop=8 changes the visual tab width},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/settings/set_tabstop`

Tests that `:set tabstop=8` changes the visual display width of tab
characters to 8 columns. The content starts with a small tabstop so the
change is clearly visible.

Ex: `:set tabstop=4` then `:set tabstop=8`

- **set_tabstop_initial.png**: Default tabstop; tab characters shown at default width.
- **set_tabstop_tabstop_4.png**: After `:set tabstop=4`, tabs are narrower (4 columns).
- **set_tabstop_tabstop_8.png**: After `:set tabstop=8`, tabs are wider (8 columns).
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->ex('set tabstop=4');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('tabstop_4');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->ex('set tabstop=8');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('tabstop_8');
    },
}
